uper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Swamp","oracle_id":"56719f6a-1a6c-4c0a-8d21-18f7d7350b68","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {B}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["B"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Swamp"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Alesha's triggered ability checks the card's power only in your graveyard. The creature will still be tapped and attacking if its power is greater than 2 after it's on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6969a7e2-6866-4001-a139-24b3be13deae","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although the returned creature is an attacking creature, it was never declared as an attacking creature. This means that abilities that trigger whenever a creature attacks won't trigger when it enters the battlefield attacking.","oracle_id":"6969a7e2-6866-4001-a139-24b3be13deae","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any effects that say that the returned creature can't attack (such as that of Propaganda, or if the creature has defender) affect only the declaration of attackers. They won't stop the returned creature from entering the battlefield attacking.","oracle_id":"6969a7e2-6866-4001-a139-24b3be13deae","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While resolving Alesha's triggered ability, you can't pay the cost multiple times to return more than one creature card.","oracle_id":"6969a7e2-6866-4001-a139-24b3be13deae","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose which player or planeswalker the returned creature is attacking. It doesn't have to be attacking the same player or planeswalker Alesha is attacking.","oracle_id":"6969a7e2-6866-4001-a139-24b3be13deae","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any spell you cast that doesn’t have the type creature will cause prowess to trigger. If a spell has multiple types, and one of those types is creature (such as an artifact creature), casting it won’t cause prowess to trigger. Playing a land also won’t cause prowess to trigger.","oracle_id":"7b22f31c-9caa-4afd-8c44-f88346bfa79c","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once it triggers, prowess isn’t connected to the spell that caused it to trigger. If that spell is countered, prowess will still resolve.","oracle_id":"7b22f31c-9caa-4afd-8c44-f88346bfa79c","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Prowess goes on the stack on top of the spell that caused it to trigger. It will resolve before that spell.","oracle_id":"7b22f31c-9caa-4afd-8c44-f88346bfa79c","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Prowess triggers only once for any spell, even if that spell has multiple types.","oracle_id":"7b22f31c-9caa-4afd-8c44-f88346bfa79c","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A legendary permanent that is put into a graveyard because of the \"legend rule\" isn't sacrificed.","oracle_id":"fe2e27a9-437e-4d22-aa22-982978793cff","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you sacrifice Kels, its middle ability triggers. It also triggers for any other creatures you sacrifice at the same time. You can sacrifice Kels to pay the cost of its own ability.","oracle_id":"fe2e27a9-437e-4d22-aa22-982978793cff","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you sacrifice a permanent as part of a spell or activated ability's cost, Kels's middle ability will resolve before that spell or ability.","oracle_id":"fe2e27a9-437e-4d22-aa22-982978793cff","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Kels's middle ability is a triggered ability, not an activated ability. It doesn't allow you to sacrifice a permanent whenever you want; rather, you need some other way of sacrificing permanents, such as Kels's last ability.","oracle_id":"fe2e27a9-437e-4d22-aa22-982978793cff","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"While resolving Kels's middle ability, you can't pay {U/B} more than once to draw more than one card.","oracle_id":"fe2e27a9-437e-4d22-aa22-982978793cff","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can activate Kels's last ability even if nothing's about to destroy it and even if it already has indestructible.","oracle_id":"fe2e27a9-437e-4d22-aa22-982978793cff","published_at":"2020-06-23","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
